==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|sweetnesse||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|swetnes}}, {{m|enm|swetnesse}}, from {{inh|en|ang|swētnes|t=sweetness}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*swōtinassī|t=sweetness}}, equivalent to {{af|en|sweet|-ness}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|swietens|t=sweetness}}, obsolete {{cog|nl|zoetenis|t=sweetness}}, {{cog|goh|swuoznessi}}, {{m|goh|suoznessi|t=sweetness}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|swēt'nəs|a=RP}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈswiːtnəs/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈswitnəs/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-sweetness.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{hyphenation|en|sweet|ness}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[condition#Noun|condition]] of being [[sweet#Adjective|sweet]] {{gl|all senses}}.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Brooke Younger|title=What Is Swicy, and Why Do You Need It in Your Life?|magazine=Cozymeal|url=https://www.cozymeal.com/magazine/swicy|date=2024-06-06|passage=At the same time, that pain is soothed by the brain’s perception of '''sweetness''' on a totally different area of your taste buds.}}
# A [[pleasant]] [[disposition]]; [[kindness]].
#: {{ux|en|Ruth's overwhelming '''sweetness''' made Robert forget about his hopelessly low school grades.}}
# The [[quality]] of giving [[pleasure]] to the [[mind]] or [[senses]], [[pleasantness]], [[agreeableness]].
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=vii|page=40|passage=The thirſt of raigne and '''ſweetnes''' of a crowne, {{...}} / Moou’d me to menage armes againſt thy ſtate.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1906|author=Violet Hunt|title=The Workaday Woman|page=1
|passage=Quiet people too, for I think that about this time a sort of remorseful tenderness comes over the bullies and the nagsters, so that they go about gently and deprecatingly, hoping by one day's record '''sweetness''' to outface the year's blusterings.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} {{n-g|A term of address for one's [[sweetheart]].}}
#* '''1986''', The Smiths (band), ''Bigmouth Strikes Again'' (song)
#*: '''Sweetness, sweetness,''' I was only joking when I said / I'd like to smash every tooth in your head.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=Kimberly Gibney|title=Over the Edge|page=66
|passage="Hey '''sweetness'''," he said. "How was practice?"}}

